 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Not necessarily bad, it just depends on where you live. How cold does it get where you ride? Then maybe a winter bike with clipless cleats. You wear shoes that clip into the pedals, so your feet don't go straight through the rubber. That' a good middle ground. A light, dry bike and a thin jacket are much easier than a full winter bike. No, but studded or studded tyres are worth look. They have small spikes that grip like mad in the slush.",
